{id:'a1',b:0,i:0,t:'Talk, watch, record',s:'Interviews, field studies, diary studies',flag:1,d:'Understand people in their own context before choosing solutions. The default SP session is 45 minutes: warm up, free exploration with think-aloud, mental model probes, clinical reflection, open reflection. No task is set.',links:[['User interviews',L('user-interviews')],['Contextual inquiry',L('contextual-inquiry')],['Field studies',L('field-studies')],['Diary studies',L('diary-studies')],['Thinking aloud',L('thinking-aloud-the-1-usability-tool')],['d.school Bootleg','https://dschool.stanford.edu/tools/design-thinking-bootleg'],['IxDF: Empathise','https://ixdf.org/literature/article/stage-1-in-the-design-thinking-process-empathise-with-your-users']]},
{id:'a2',b:0,i:1,t:'Sort and name',s:'Card sorting, mental models, concept tests',d:'Find out how people group and name things and what they believe the platform is, before changing structure or labels. Follow card sorting with tree testing once a structure exists.',links:[['Card sorting',L('card-sorting-definition')],['Tree testing',L('tree-testing')],['Mental models',L('mental-models')],['Desirability reaction words',L('desirability-reaction-words')]]},
