{id:'a4',b:0,i:3,t:'Insights, hypotheses',s:'Proposed, not yet tested',d:'Write insight statements: [category] needs [need] because [reason]. Record any idea as a Proposed hypothesis. Nothing from this band is reported as a percentage or as proof.',links:[]},
{id:'b1',b:1,i:0,t:'Ideate',s:'How Might We, design options',d:'Turn insight into open design questions and options. Psychology offers a short sourced rationale on contested or clinically sensitive choices.',links:[['How Might We questions',L('how-might-we-questions')]]},
{id:'b2',b:1,i:1,t:'Design hypothesis',s:'Belief, outcome, signal',d:'We believe [design decision] will achieve [outcome] for [participants]. We will know this is true when [signal reaches threshold]. The primary measure, target and minimum acceptable value are chosen now.',links:[['Lean UX hypothesis format','https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/designing-for-product/9781491971451/ch05.html']]},
{id:'b3',b:1,i:2,t:'Prototype',s:'Paper to high fidelity',d:'Make the idea testable. Privacy and visibility cues are built in so people can see, not infer, what is private.',links:[['Paper prototyping',L('paper-prototyping')]]},
{id:'c1',b:2,i:0,t:'Pre-check',s:'Heuristics, walkthrough, pilot',d:'Two reviewers check the design against heuristics, including health context heuristics, then a pilot session catches broken tasks. Fix obvious problems first so participants are not spent on them.',links:[['Heuristic evaluation',L('how-to-conduct-a-heuristic-evaluation')],['Ten heuristics',L('ten-usability-heuristics')],['Inspection methods',L('summary-of-usability-inspection-methods')]]},
{id:'c2',b:2,i:1,t:'Register hypothesis',s:'Criteria and decision rule, locked',d:'Lock the hypothesis, tasks, measures, sample and decision rule before the first session. Later changes need a dated amendment with a reason. This is what keeps the study confirmatory.',links:[['Confounding variables',L('confounding-variables-quantitative-ux')],['Internal vs external validity',L('internal-vs-external-validity')]]},
{id:'c3',b:2,i:2,t:'Run the test',s:'Usability, benchmark, compare, clinical review',flag:1,d:'Moderated task-based sessions with a written scenario per feature behaviour, think-aloud and no facilitator help. Alongside, two Psychology reviewers rate the feature against the clinical appropriateness rubric. A Not appropriate result blocks release.',links:[['Usability testing 101',L('usability-testing-101')],['Task scenarios',L('task-scenarios-usability-testing')],['Better tasks',L('better-usability-tasks')],['Leading questions',L('leading-questions')]]},
{id:'c4',b:2,i:3,t:'Measure and decide',s:'Behaviour plus attitude, intervals',d:'Report behaviour and attitude together, with a 95% confidence interval. Confirmed if the lower bound clears the minimum acceptable value; Not confirmed if the upper bound falls below it; otherwise Inconclusive. With 20 participants, 19 successes are needed for the lower bound to reach 70%.',links:[['Quantitative study guide',L('quantitative-research-study-guide')],['Usability metrics',L('usability-metrics')],['Measuring perceived usability',L('measuring-perceived-usability')]]},
{id:'d1',b:3,i:0,t:'Synthesis session',s:'Biweekly, exploratory and confirmatory apart',d:'Psychology, Design and Tech review evidence together. Exploratory and confirmatory items are separate agenda items and never blended. Exploratory findings can come here directly from the Understand band.',links:[]},
{id:'d2',b:3,i:1,t:'Decision and owner',s:'Accept, reject, or research more',d:'Every actionable finding gets a decision, a named owner and a status. Where disciplines read the evidence differently, the difference is recorded. Who holds final authority to prioritise is still to be confirmed.',links:[]},
{id:'d3',b:3,i:2,t:'Tech implements',s:'Writes status back in writing',d:'Tech makes the agreed change and writes the implementation status back after every synthesis session. This is the step most likely to be skipped and the one most responsible for lost trust in feedback.',links:[]},
{id:'d4',b:3,i:3,t:'Retest trigger',s:'Change, ageing, live-use problems',d:'Retest when the tested flow changes, a confirmed result ages, a severity 3 or 4 problem appears in live use, the user population changes, or an earlier result was inconclusive.',links:[]}];
